name: Marked scope boundaries, exact six-job approval and per-scope recurrence
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/finite_scopes.py @TMP_TARGET @ART seed @TMP_HOME
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: setg ui.auto_open_activity false
submit: setg ui.auto_open_viz false
submit: logs
submit: run context:build {"enrichment":false}
require-live-snap: 35 Build project context: | source-context
submit: use threat-model
submit: options threat-model:import
submit: set path .kuzushi/manual-scope-context.json
submit: set activate false
submit: set label Owned scope study source
submit: run threat-model:import
require-live-snap: 35 threat-model:import saved | map-context
submit: map
require-live-snap: 25 SYSTEM SUMMARY | map-result
nav-mode:
keys: u
require-live-snap: 25 Map ✓ | accepted-map
submit: scopes
require-live-snap: 30 ACCEPTED SCOPES | accepted-scopes
keys: Space Down Space
require-live-snap: 20 2 boundaries marked | marked-boundaries
ask: Can the operator mark only the intended discovery boundaries while shared context and unplanned siblings remain distinguishable?
keys: p
require-live-snap: 30 PLAN A STUDY | scope-study
keys: Down Down Enter
require-live-snap: 20 CHOOSE DISCOVERY ENGINES | engine-choice
keys: m
keys: Down Down Down Down Down Down Down Down Down Space
require-live-snap: 20 [x] agentic | selected-agentic
keys: a
require-live-snap: 20 Engine choices updated | selected-engine
keys: Down
require-live-snap: 20 Selected boundaries: 2 | selected-workload
expect: 6 fixed discovery jobs
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 SCOPE CONTEXT | boundary-context
keys: Down Enter Enter
require-live-snap: 25 CONTEXT SUMMARY | common-context-preview
keys: e
require-live-snap: 20 ↑↓ Enter edit | context-editor-ready
keys: Enter C-u
type: APP_ONLY_CONTEXT_BOUNDARY. This owned App context is source guidance, not a finding verdict. Shared files provide context only.
keys: C-s
require-live-snap: 20 REVIEW CONTEXT CHANGES | context-copy-review
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 30 Edited copy saved | inactive-context-copy
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 APP_ONLY_CONTEXT_BOUNDARY | edited-context-preview
keys: a
require-live-snap: 20 Context selected for app | boundary-context-selected
expect: app · exact override
expect: other · inherits common
ask: Can the operator inspect and select an inactive local context for App while Other inherits the accepted common revision, without changing global context or starting work?
keys: Escape
require-live-snap: 20 PLAN A STUDY | scoped-context-draft
keys: Down Down Enter
type: 8
keys: Enter Down Enter
type: 2
keys: Enter L
require-live-snap: 30 Scope draft ready | frozen-plan
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/finite_scopes.py @TMP_TARGET @ART draft
keys: L Home
require-live-snap: 30 REVIEW PLAN & ALLOWANCE | exact-allowance
expect: 6 fixed jobs
expect: Total provider calls: 8
expect: Protected review calls: 2
keys: End
require-live-snap: 30 y approve | exact-approval
ask: Does approval show all six finite jobs and the shared allowance before any request, without approving sibling or follow-up work?
keys: y
require-live-snap: 30 Approval saved | approved
keys: L
require-live-snap: 30 L starts its fixed jobs | fixed-jobs
keys: L
require-live-snap: 30 dispatcher pid | running
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/finite_scopes.py @TMP_TARGET @ART completed
keys: r
require-live-snap: 30 6 completed | completed
keys: Escape
submit: workbench
require-live-snap: 30 Viewing Scan | scan-result
nav-mode:
keys: n
require-live-snap: 30 Viewing Review | accepted-scan
keys: Escape
submit: scopes
require-live-snap: 25 ACCEPTED SCOPES | scope-findings-origin
keys: Home v
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/finite_scopes.py @TMP_TARGET @ART scope-review-frame
require-live-snap: 25 scope app · exact record · 3 runs | app-scope-findings
expect: q scopes
expect: Labeled app observation
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/finite_scopes.py @TMP_TARGET @ART scope-checked
resize: 160x48
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/finite_scopes.py @TMP_TARGET @ART scope-review-frame
require-live-snap: 25 scope app · exact record | scope-findings-160x48
resize: 96x89
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/finite_scopes.py @TMP_TARGET @ART scope-review-frame
require-live-snap: 25 scope app · exact record | scope-findings-96x89
resize: 80x24
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/finite_scopes.py @TMP_TARGET @ART scope-review-frame
require-live-snap: 25 scope app · exact record | scope-findings-80x24
resize: 60x20
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/finite_scopes.py @TMP_TARGET @ART scope-review-frame
require-live-snap: 25 scope app · exact record | scope-findings-60x20
resize: 40x12
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/finite_scopes.py @TMP_TARGET @ART scope-review-frame
require-live-snap: 25 scope app · exact record | scope-findings-40x12
expect: q scopes
resize: 120x36
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/finite_scopes.py @TMP_TARGET @ART scope-review-frame
require-live-snap: 25 scope app · exact record | scope-findings-120x36
ask: Is the exact saved scope clear, and can the operator read App's consolidated finding without starting another scan or losing the marked boundaries?
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/finite_scopes.py @TMP_TARGET @ART scope-hide
submit: findings refresh
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/finite_scopes.py @TMP_TARGET @ART scope-partial-frame
require-live-snap: 25 partial scope app · 1 unread · 2 runs | unread-scope-evidence
expect: Labeled app observation
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/finite_scopes.py @TMP_TARGET @ART scope-hidden
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/finite_scopes.py @TMP_TARGET @ART scope-restore
submit: findings refresh
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/finite_scopes.py @TMP_TARGET @ART scope-review-frame
require-live-snap: 25 scope app · exact record · 3 runs | restored-scope-evidence
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/finite_scopes.py @TMP_TARGET @ART scope-restored
nav-mode:
keys: q
require-live-snap: 25 ACCEPTED SCOPES | scope-findings-return
keys: Down Enter /
type: View saved findings
require-live-snap: 20 ▸ View saved findings | saved-findings-action
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/finite_scopes.py @TMP_TARGET @ART scope-action-help
keys: Enter
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/finite_scopes.py @TMP_TARGET @ART scope-other-frame
require-live-snap: 25 scope other · exact record · 3 runs | other-scope-findings
expect: Labeled other observation
ask: Does unreadable scope evidence remain visibly partial, recover without rewriting it, and return to the prior boundary before opening its sibling?
keys: q
require-live-snap: 25 Search: View saved findings | saved-findings-action-return
keys: Escape Escape
require-live-snap: 25 ACCEPTED SCOPES | other-scope-return
keys: Escape
paste-file: @ART/open-app.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 30 Labeled app observation | app-finding
submit: dismiss false_positive Owned workflow fixture; no defect claimed
require-live-snap: 30 rejected_false_positive | app-decision
paste-file: @ART/open-other.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 30 Labeled other observation | other-finding
submit: dismiss false_positive Owned workflow fixture; no defect claimed
require-live-snap: 30 rejected_false_positive | other-decision
submit: report
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/finite_scopes.py @TMP_TARGET @ART scope-report-frame
require-live-snap: 30 Scope study: | scope-report
expect: Scope study: 2 boundaries · 1 unplanned
expect: 6 committed / 8 calls
expect: 2 protected review remaining
expect: 3 completed / 3 planned
expect: Unplanned boundaries: integration
ask: Does the report retain separate three-pass scope denominators, shared spending and the unplanned boundary, with no complete coverage claim?
keys: j j j
require-live-snap: 20 format json (4/6) | json-format
keys: Enter End
require-live-snap: 30 json · 2 finding(s) | scoped-export
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/finite_scopes.py @TMP_TARGET @ART exported
keys: p Home
resize: 160x48
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/finite_scopes.py @TMP_TARGET @ART scope-report-frame
require-live-snap: 25 format json (4/6) · all | report-160x48
expect: Study id:
